 "captions": [
  {
   "start_s": 0.3,
   "end_s": 3.97,
   "text": "This is a real table tennis rally, from a game our model never saw in training."
  },
  {
   "start_s": 4.09,
   "end_s": 7.62,
   "text": "It calls this shot a miss 408 milliseconds before the ball gets there."
  },
  {
   "start_s": 7.74,
   "end_s": 11.82,
   "text": "Courtside asks what that head start is worth on a prediction market, and what we can prove."
  },
  {
   "start_s": 12.42,
   "end_s": 14.59,
   "text": "When a point ends, the news spreads in tiers."
  },
  {
   "start_s": 14.71,
   "end_s": 18.41,
   "text": "A courtside camera with our vision model would know in about 95 milliseconds."
  },
  {
   "start_s": 18.53,
   "end_s": 23.88,
   "text": "ESPN's live score trails the order book by about 28 seconds, the public scoreboard by 45."
  },
  {
   "start_s": 24.0,
   "end_s": 29.48,
   "text": "Slower tiers trade against stale prices. The gap persists because speed costs money, and capacity is small."
  },
  {
   "start_s": 30.08,
   "end_s": 33.32,
   "text": "A small group of wallets trades in the first three seconds after a point."
  },
  {
   "start_s": 33.44,
   "end_s": 38.62,
   "text": "Thirty seconds later, net of fees, they are up in 9 of 9 months. Everyone else is down in 9."
  },
  {
   "start_s": 38.75,
   "end_s": 43.02,
   "text": "Copying them three seconds later loses in 9 of 9. The edge goes to whoever is first."
  },
  {
   "start_s": 43.62,
   "end_s": 45.14,
   "text": "So we built our own fast tier."
  },
  {
   "start_s": 45.26,
   "end_s": 48.81,
   "text": "On held-out games, it tracks the ball and calls misses before contact."
  },
  {
   "start_s": 48.93,
   "end_s": 55.75,
   "text": "Fifty milliseconds out, it made 11 calls, all correct. The 95% lower bound on precision is 74 percent."
  },
  {
   "start_s": 55.87,
   "end_s": 59.46,
   "text": "It catches 27 percent of misses that early, and leaves the rest alone."
  },
  {
   "start_s": 60.06,
   "end_s": 63.78,
   "text": "We have no licensed tennis footage, so this replay is simulated physics."
  },
  {
   "start_s": 63.9,
   "end_s": 69.94,
   "text": "A 340 frame per second tracker calls it out 200 milliseconds before the bounce, and reads the spin from the flight."
  },
  {
   "start_s": 70.06,
   "end_s": 74.45,
   "text": "On the right is a real Polymarket tape: fast-tier wallets traded within seconds of the point."
  },
  {
   "start_s": 75.05,
   "end_s": 78.74,
   "text": "Version two trades only at the fast tier's own fill prices, after fees."
  },
  {
   "start_s": 78.86,
   "end_s": 86.09,
   "text": "In sample, February to August: 1.38 cents a share, Sharpe 14.5, worst drawdown 2.0 percent."
  },
  {
   "start_s": 86.21,
   "end_s": 91.68,
   "text": "Out of sample, a window we had already seen: 0.60 cents, Sharpe 6.7."
  },
  {
   "start_s": 91.8,
   "end_s": 96.12,
   "text": "Double the fees, and out of sample turns negative: \u22120.34 cents."
  },
  {
   "start_s": 96.72,
   "end_s": 100.29,
   "text": "We tried thousands of configurations, so we deflate the Sharpe ratio."
  },
  {
   "start_s": 100.41,
   "end_s": 105.85,
   "text": "In sample it stays above 0.99, even counting all 3,386 trials."
  },
  {
   "start_s": 105.97,
   "end_s": 110.59,
   "text": "The 40-day out-of-sample window does not survive that. It falls to 0.07."
  },
  {
   "start_s": 110.71,
   "end_s": 114.78,
   "text": "Probability of backtest overfitting on the 24-variant grid: 15 percent."
  },
  {
   "start_s": 115.38,
   "end_s": 120.87,
   "text": "Unseen markets passed in sample, then failed out of sample. The market-making variant failed its blind test."
  },
  {
   "start_s": 120.99,
   "end_s": 123.3,
   "text": "Table tennis markets had no fast tier at all."
  },
  {
   "start_s": 123.42,
   "end_s": 128.47,
   "text": "The blind forward test is still pending. Every look at out-of-sample data is logged: 51 entries."
  },
  {
   "start_s": 129.07,
   "end_s": 131.76,
   "text": "What does vision buy? This part is a counterfactual."
  },
  {
   "start_s": 131.88,
   "end_s": 136.32,
   "text": "It assumes a licensed feed and a courtside camera we did not buy, with parameters we measured."
  },
  {
   "start_s": 136.44,
   "end_s": 144.17,
   "text": "In sample, 1.10 cents a share, Sharpe 11.4. Out of sample, 0.58 cents, Sharpe 7.3."
  },
  {
   "start_s": 144.29,
   "end_s": 148.62,
   "text": "The sign hinges on how fast the market reprices after the bounce, which we have not measured."
  },
  {
   "start_s": 148.74,
   "end_s": 152.98,
   "text": "Under the stamp reading, if that takes less than 1.1 seconds, the edge is gone."
  },
  {
   "start_s": 153.58,
   "end_s": 157.12,
   "text": "The engine runs end to end on live Polymarket order books, paper only."
  },
  {
   "start_s": 157.24,
   "end_s": 162.58,
   "text": "In a 60 second check it read 7,785 book messages across 27 markets,"
  },
  {
   "start_s": 162.7,
   "end_s": 167.71,
   "text": "at a median feed latency of 65 milliseconds, with zero mismatches and zero orders sent."
  },
  {
   "start_s": 167.83,
   "end_s": 169.82,
   "text": "Tonight's live paper session is running now."
  },
  {
   "start_s": 170.42,
   "end_s": 176.67,
   "text": "In sample, a gross edge of 282 dollars a day loses 86 to taker fees, leaving 196."
  },
  {
   "start_s": 176.79,
   "end_s": 184.39,
   "text": "Central fixed costs, mostly a data licence, are 167 a day. That leaves 29 in sample, and a loss out of sample."
  },
  {
   "start_s": 184.51,
   "end_s": 189.04,
   "text": "Out of sample, the edge stays positive only up to about 34 thousand dollars of capital."
  },
  {
   "start_s": 189.16,
   "end_s": 192.98,
   "text": "Kill switches stop trading on a drawdown, a stale feed, or a fee change."
  },
  {
   "start_s": 193.58,
   "end_s": 199.3,
   "text": "Everything here is paper trading. No real money was traded, and no live ATP or WTA data was used."
  },
  {
   "start_s": 199.42,
   "end_s": 204.28,
   "text": "The code and every result file are in the public repository. One command rebuilds the backtest tables."
  }
 ],
